    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/COR1036CORN/JobBoard/30d770d7-3983-4bf1-867a-479db251bad8/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=a95f1b3b-ae05-4c0d-aa20-b4ccfff76d08": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Kinesiology (Part-time)",
      "description": "Lecturer in Kinesiology (Part-time) | Career Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Lecturer in Kinesiology (Part-time) Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on October 8, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA +0 more locations less locations Faculty Part-Time Requisition #: LECTU001431 Description Cornell College, a private undergraduate liberal arts college in Mount Vernon, Iowa, is seeking a Lecturer(s) in Kinesiology for 1 section of KIN 101 (Lifetime Physical Fitness and Activities) from March 15th-April 7th 2027.  A Ph.D. in Kinesiology or a closely related field is preferred; candidates with at least a master’s degree in Kinesiology or a closely related field will also be considered.  Experience in teaching at the college level is strongly preferred. Course and term dates: Because Cornell utilizes a block schedule for its courses, you would teach one course full time during the four-week sessions. The following is a course description: KIN 101 - Lifetime Physical Fitness and Activities (March 15-April 7) Instruction in the major components of fitness, the physiological basis of fitness, evaluation of personal fitness, and individual fitness programming. Exploration of the intersection of diet, stress, resilience, and physical activity on health. Instruction and participation in lifetime physical activities including designing and engaging in strength/resistance training, flexibility, and cardiovascular exercise, and lifestyle fitness. The college encourages interdisciplinary interests among its faculty and the development of teaching strategies that capitalize on our distinctive academic calendar. One Course At A Time allows us the freedom to take students off-campus without impinging on other course commitments. About Cornell College Cornell College is a national liberal arts college committed to excellence in teaching and the creation of a welcoming community in which all individuals are respected and included. Our innovative curriculum includes a focus on the essential abilities of writing, quantitative reasoning, and intercultural literacy as well as experiential learning. The One Course At A Time approach fosters strong student engagement and close faculty-student relationships while allowing faculty freedom to design and carry out their classes, on campus or off. Founded in 1853, Cornell was the first college west of the Mississippi to graduate both men and women.  Academic immersion, real world experience requirements through Ingenuity in Action, and unparalleled flexibility attract an ambitious student body from around the world.  Seventy percent of our students are from outside Iowa, representing nearly 50 states and 27 foreign countries. Students of color comprise one-fourth of the student body. Cornell’s picturesque hilltop campus is a National Historic District and was the first campus listed in its entirety on the National Register of Historic Places. Mount Vernon is a small, college-centered town in the Cedar Rapids-Iowa City corridor, home to nearly half a million people. It has two additional National Historic Districts and a classic Main Street a short walk from campus. Mount Vernon attractions include boutique shopping; walking paths; a dedicated sledding hill; and 13 annual festivals and events including Chalk the Walk, Chili Cookoff, and Magical Mount Vernon. Interested applicants should submit the following materials through Cornell College’s online application system: A letter of application/cover letter Current Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information for a minimum of two references. Applications will be reviewed as submitted and continue until the position is filled. Any questions can be directed to Justus Hallam, Chair of Kinesiology at jhallam@cornellcollege.edu. Cornell is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from underrepresented groups. Cornell complies with Iowa's Smoke-free Air Act. Cornell utilizes E-Verify and requires the satisfactory completion of a background check. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws.\nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. About Us You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/COR1036CORN/JobBoard/30d770d7-3983-4bf1-867a-479db251bad8/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=076d9fb5-bd98-4777-954e-cef2b3e72a38": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Creative Writing (Poetry) (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Creative Writing (Poetry) (Tenure-Track) | Career Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Assistant Professor of Creative Writing (Poetry) (Tenure-Track) Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on October 7, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA +0 more locations less locations Faculty Full-Time Requisition #: ASSIS001430 Description The Department of English and Creative Writing at Cornell College invites applications for a tenure-track (Assistant Professor) position with a primary specialization in poetry to begin August 2027.  We seek a poet with expertise and passion for both creative writing and the literary study of 20th and 21st century anglophone poetry.  Desirable secondary interests may include one or more of the following: nature writing, video game writing, creative writing as social action, literary translation, hybrid writing, new media writing, writing for the artist book, writing for children, multicultural literature, disability studies, and/or genre fiction.  The successful candidate will join a dynamic department committed to innovative teaching, creative expression, close mentorship, and inclusivity.  All faculty in the department participate in the activities of our thriving Center for the Literary Arts.  We have a proud history of student literary publications, more recently augmented by book-arts work enabled by our historic iron handpress. Teaching responsibilities include contributions to the first-year college writing program, an introductory multigenre creative writing workshop, upper-division workshops in poetry, courses focused on the literary study of poetry (e.g. Modernisms, Contemporary Poetry or special topics), and courses in the individual’s secondary expertise. Required qualifications: PhD in creative writing (poetry or related field) or an MFA (poetry) with extensive teaching experience evidence of effective, student-centered undergraduate teaching experience in creative writing, literature, and composition an active publication agenda in poetry Preferred qualifications: evidence of effective engagement with a diverse student body experience of inclusive approaches to mentoring evidence of contributing to and promoting a diverse literary community Cornell’s One Course At A Time academic calendar is divided into eight 3½ week blocks in which students take and faculty teach a single course. Full-time faculty teaching load is six block courses during the academic year with the other two blocks reserved for professional development, course preparation, or travel to academic meetings; further opportunities for summer teaching and research supervision may also be available. Candidates will be expected to participate in service to their department and to facilitate their department’s support of the college’s Ingenuity core curriculum.  The college encourages interdisciplinary interests among its faculty and the development of teaching strategies that capitalize on our distinctive academic calendar. One Course At A Time allows us the freedom to take students off-campus without impinging on other course commitments. In addition, class size is limited to 25 students, and writing-intensive courses are smaller. About Cornell College Cornell College is a national liberal arts college committed to excellence in teaching and the creation of a welcoming community in which all individuals are respected and included. Our innovative curriculum includes a focus on the essential abilities of writing, quantitative reasoning, and intercultural literacy as well as experiential learning. The One Course At A Time approach fosters strong student engagement and close faculty-student relationships while allowing faculty freedom to design and carry out their classes, on campus or off. Founded in 1853, Cornell was the first college west of the Mississippi to graduate both men and women.  Academic immersion, real world experience requirements through Ingenuity in Action, and unparalleled flexibility attract an ambitious student body from around the world. Cornell’s picturesque hilltop campus is a National Historic District and was the first campus listed in its entirety on the National Register of Historic Places. Mount Vernon is a small, college-centered town in the Cedar Rapids-Iowa City corridor, home to nearly half a million people. It has two additional National Historic Districts and a classic Main Street a short walk from campus. Mount Vernon attractions include boutique shopping; walking paths; a dedicated sledding hill; and 13 annual festivals and events including Chalk the Walk, Chili Cookoff, and Magical Mount Vernon. Cornell College offers a competitive benefits package that includes health, dental, vision, HSA and FSA accounts, a TIAA 403(b) retirement account, and tuition remission and exchange for employees and dependents. We also offer life insurance, disability insurance, travel insurance, and accident insurance. Interested applicants should submit the following materials through Cornell College’s online application system: A letter of application/cover letter Current Curriculum Vitae Graduate transcript(s) (may be unofficial) Teaching statement, describing teaching interests, experience, and philosophy, including examples of inclusive pedagogy Names and contact information for a minimum of three references. Formal letters will be requested at a later date. A ten-page selection of creative work (poetry) Applications will be reviewed beginning November 9, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be legally authorized to work for any employer in the United States at the time of hire and throughout employment. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. For more information about the department, please visit the departmental website https://www.cornellcollege.edu/english-and-creative-writing/ Any questions can be directed to Katie Sagal, Department Chair and Associate Professor of English & Creative Writing at asagal@cornellcollege.edu . Cornell is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from underrepresented groups. Cornell complies with Iowa’s Smoke-free Air Act. Cornell utilizes E-Verify and requires the satisfactory completion of a background check. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws.\nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. About Us You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/COR1036CORN/JobBoard/30d770d7-3983-4bf1-867a-479db251bad8/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=31387143-5bbb-4ad2-849b-e154779b8b55": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Associate Registrar | Career Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Associate Registrar Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on October 7, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA +0 more locations less locations Program Support Full-Time Requisition #: ASSOC001429 Description Cornell College invites applications for an associate registrar. The associate registrar is responsible for working with faculty, staff, and students to guide them through the registration process, maintain and update the Academic Catalog, and work with students on degree audits and Commencement responsibilities.  The position serves as a source of information and answers questions for all constituents on academic policies and procedures as well as degree and major requirements. Duties/Responsibilities Work with the Registrar and academic departments to maintain and update the Academic Catalogue. Is responsible for assigning course numbers to new courses and updating major/minor checklists in multiple locations. Serve students and faculty by answering questions, explaining regulations and procedures, interpreting the Catalogue, and providing necessary resources. Assign classrooms each block and make adjustments as needed. Maintain system of keeping track of classrooms and their attributes. Serve as a member of the Academic Programs committee and is responsible for making changes to academic programs in the Catalogue, PowerCampus, and Stellic degree audit software. Assist with maintenance of student records and major declarations, and assist in the coordination of the registration process. Guide students and faculty through the transfer of credit process, and track and record transfer courses on students’ records. Work with the Registrar to evaluate transfer courses from other institutions on an ongoing basis. Is the primary contact for degree audits, and is responsible for the logistics of degree completion and communicating with seniors about degree audits and progress. Works with non-graduates on completing degree requirements after Commencement. Represents the Registrar’s Office on the campus Commencement committee and is responsible for maintaining an ongoing list of graduating seniors, monitoring degree progress, and working with the Office of Marketing and Communication to develop the Commencement program. Work with the Athletic department to determine athletic eligibility and calculate team GPAs as needed for athletic awards. With the Assistant Registrar, maintain the web site for the Registrar’s office. Supervise 3-5 student workers Serve as customer service front line staff member as needed. Is the primary contact for use of the Stellic degree audit software and serves as the campus contact for the Stellic team. Makes updates to Stellic audits, is responsible for creating instructions and instructional videos, and assists students and advisors in effectively using the software. Work with faculty to track and record adjunct courses and topics course offerings Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) to support international student advising on immigrations matters within Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS) Other duties as assigned. About Cornell College Cornell College is a selective liberal arts college distinguished by our Ingenuity curriculum that builds on the strengths of our One Course At A Time schedule. This combination encourages the qualities of being thoughtful, original, and inventive, using the strengths of a liberal arts education to apply ideas to solve problems and meet challenges through hands-on experience in learning. Academic immersion, Division III NCAA athletic teams, and unparalleled flexibility attract an ambitious student body from across the U.S. and worldwide. We are located in Mount Vernon, Iowa, an urban fringe community located in the heart of the ICR Iowa region. Qualifications and Education Requirements Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and work experience required.  Experience in higher education preferred. Preferred Skills Knowledge of general office procedures and the ability to use office equipment such as copiers, calculators, and computer software including MS Office applications. Ability to learn new software such as cms, PowerCampus, and other tools as needed.  Ability to communicate effectively and interact professionally in a variety of situations in person and on the telephone.   Ability to multi-task and work in a fast-paced environment with multiple interruptions.  Commitment to maintaining confidentiality. Demonstrated customer-service orientation. Fine finger movement is required for typing, word processing and filing, as well as reaching and grasping. Working Conditions Work is performed primarily while seated in an office environment with some walking from building to building for various meetings. Cornell College complies with federal and state disability laws and makes reasonable accommodations for applicants and employees with disabilities. If reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other benefits and privileges of employment, please contact human_resources@cornellcollege.edu. Cornell employees enjoy a fantastic benefits package that includes health, dental, vision, HSA & FSA accounts, a TIAA 403(b) retirement account, and tuition remission and exchange for employees and dependents. The college also offers life insurance, disability insurance, travel insurance, and accident insurance. And, all full-time staff begin with a 4-week vacation accrual along with 14.5 paid holidays per year.  The hiring pay range for the position is $48,000 - $55,000. Application Process To apply, submit a resume, cover letter, and list of at least three professional references through Cornell College's online application system. Cornell is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from underrepresented groups. Cornell complies with Iowa's Smoke-free Air Act. Cornell utilizes E-Verify and requires the satisfactory completion of a background check. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws.\nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. About Us You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/COR1036CORN/JobBoard/30d770d7-3983-4bf1-867a-479db251bad8/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=6787383f-b30b-46dd-9a49-38158bf88d36": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Chemistry (Tenure-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Chemistry (Tenure-Track) | Career Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Assistant Professor in Chemistry (Tenure-Track) Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on September 24, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA +0 more locations less locations Faculty Full-Time Requisition #: ASSIS001427 Description Cornell College, a residential undergraduate liberal arts college, invites applications for a tenure-track appointment as Assistant Professor in its ACS-approved Department of Chemistry beginning Fall 2027.  Primary teaching responsibilities will be a combination of organic and general chemistry courses, including an advanced organic course in rotation, and participation in the college’s core curriculum.  The Department of Chemistry has a strong history of student/faculty research, and engagement in research with students is expected.  PhD is required. Cornell’s One Course At A Time academic calendar is divided into eight 3½ week blocks in which students take and faculty teach a single course. Full-time faculty teaching load is 6 block courses during the academic year with the other 2 blocks reserved for professional development, course preparations, or travel to academic meetings; further opportunities for summer teaching and research supervision may also be available. Candidate will be expected to participate in service to their department and to facilitate their department’s support of the college’s Ingenuity core curriculum.  The college encourages interdisciplinary interests among its faculty and the development of teaching strategies that capitalize on our distinctive academic calendar. One Course At A Time allows us the freedom to take students off-campus without impinging on other course commitments. In addition, class size is limited to 25 students, and upper-level courses are often smaller. About Cornell College Cornell College is a national liberal arts college committed to excellence in teaching and the creation of a welcoming community in which all individuals are respected and included. Our innovative curriculum includes a focus on the essential abilities of writing, quantitative reasoning, and intercultural literacy as well as experiential learning. The One Course At A Time approach fosters strong student engagement and close faculty-student relationships while allowing faculty freedom to design and carry out their classes, on campus or off. Founded in 1853, Cornell was the first college west of the Mississippi to graduate both men and women.  Academic immersion, real world experience requirements through Ingenuity in Action, and unparalleled flexibility attract an ambitious student body from around the world. Cornell’s picturesque hilltop campus is a National Historic District and was the first campus listed in its entirety on the National Register of Historic Places. Mount Vernon is a small, college-centered town in the Cedar Rapids-Iowa City corridor, home to nearly half a million people. It has two additional National Historic Districts and a classic Main Street a short walk from campus. Mount Vernon attractions include boutique shopping; walking paths; a dedicated sledding hill; and 13 annual festivals and events including Chalk the Walk, Chili Cookoff, and Magical Mount Vernon. Cornell College offers a competitive benefits package that includes health, dental, vision, HSA and FSA accounts, a TIAA 403(b) retirement account, and tuition remission and exchange for employees and dependents. We also offer life insurance, disability insurance, travel insurance, and accident insurance. Interested applicants should submit the following materials through Cornell College’s online application system: A letter of application/cover letter Current Curriculum Vitae Graduate transcript(s) (may be unofficial) Teaching statement, describing teaching interests, experience, and philosophy, including examples of inclusive pedagogy Names and contact information for a minimum of three references. Formal letters will be requested at a later date. Applications will be reviewed beginning October 19, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be legally authorized to work for any employer in the United States at the time of hire and throughout employment. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. For more information about the department, please visit the Chemistry department website . Any questions can be directed to Cindy Strong, Department Chair and William Deskin Professor of Chemistry at cstrong@cornellcollege.edu Cornell is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from underrepresented groups. Cornell complies with Iowa’s Smoke-free Air Act. Cornell utilizes E-Verify and requires the satisfactory completion of a background check. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws.\nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. About Us You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
