    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/COR1036CORN/JobBoard/30d770d7-3983-4bf1-867a-479db251bad8/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=6ac8bb33-39b2-4e39-b123-e13ccef8064e": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Berry Career Institute",
      "description": "Associate Director, Berry Career Institute | Career Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Associate Director, Berry Career Institute Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on September 21, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA +0 more locations less locations On-site Program Support Full-Time Requisition #: ASSOC001424 Description Cornell College invites applications for an Associate Director, Berry Career Institute. The Associate Director directly serves students and plays an important role in the day-to-day operations of the Berry Career Institute. The Berry Career Institute (BCI) is part of the division of Alumni and College Advancement, positioning career outcomes as a central strategic priority that connects the student experience to graduate careers, alumni engagement, and the long-term reputation of a Cornell College education. The Associate Director coaches students, facilitates programs, and contributes to the broader career-learning initiatives of the college to ensure that all students are given opportunities to develop the skills and perspective needed to navigate the world of work and apply their liberal arts education beyond the classroom. Duties and Responsibilities Student & Alumni Career Coaching : Primarily serves as the point of contact for a portfolio of current students and alumni to provide career coaching and professional development support in individual and group settings. Develops relationships with students and alumni to connect them to resources and opportunities to achieve employment or other post-graduation success such as continuing education, fellowships, or service. Creates and maintains career coaching resources and materials. Develops opportunities to connect alumni to current students through networking and mentoring. Stays up-to-date on industry and employer trends to help students navigate a changing employment landscape and best apply their liberal arts education to their life beyond Cornell College. Program Facilitation : Designs, facilitates, and promotes a variety of programs with internal and external partners to increase career-readiness, vocational discernment, professional development, and related skills among students across the College. Programs may include workshops and trainings inside the classroom in partnership with faculty, or programs may include events outside of the classroom such as tablings, large-scale expos or fairs, panels, guest speakers, webinars, or off campus trips such as employer tours. Experiential Learning Development : Contributes to the development and implementation of an internship program for students by identifying and cultivating relationships with potential employer partners. Develops experiential learning opportunities for students with employers. Directs students in how to find and secure internships. Helps students fund and document their experiential learning through Cornell College’s Ingenuity in Action program. Data Management and Reporting: Helps maintain information systems (i.e. Handshake) to ensure the BCI accurately tracks student and employer engagement as well as career-related learning outcomes. Contributes to the development and assessment of career learning outcomes. Sources student outcomes for priority reports such as the First Destination Survey. Identifies stories and qualitative data to be shared in BCI and College reporting and marketing. Campus-Wide Support : Serves on workgroups and supports campus-wide initiatives by collaborating with faculty and campus partners to advance career-readiness and experiential learning throughout the curriculum and College culture. Other Duties as Assigned Qualification and Education Requirements Bachelor's degree is required. Master’s degree or other training related to higher education administration, student development, counseling, or another area relevant to student engagement is preferred. Previous experience with career development and work in a college setting is preferred. Must possess a valid Iowa driver’s license and be insurable to drive. Preferred Skills Evidence of strong interpersonal and written and verbal communication skills, including facilitation skills such as designing and leading content for a variety of audiences and learning styles Knowledge of student development practices (prior student advising or coaching and mentoring experience a plus) Organization and planning skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and constituents, including event planning and program development and assessment Strong team player with the ability to collaborate effectively across departments Understanding of data management best practices and attention to detail Dedication to liberal arts education Awareness of human resources, recruitment, and hiring practices Work Location & Conditions Work is performed primarily while seated in an office environment. Some walking from building to building on campus is needed to attend various meetings. Employees may be required to perform other job-related duties as assigned. All requirements are subject to change over time, with possible modifications made to reasonably accommodate individuals with a disability. Cornell College offers a fantastic benefits package that includes health, dental, vision, HSA & FSA accounts, a TIAA 403(b) retirement account, and tuition remission and exchange for employees and dependents. We also offer life insurance, disability insurance, travel insurance, and accident insurance. And, all full-time staff begin with a 4-week vacation accrual along with 14.5 paid holidays per year. The hiring pay range for this position is $42,000 - $48,000. Application Process To apply, submit a resume, cover letter, and list of at least three professional references through Cornell College's online application system. Cornell is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from underrepresented groups. Cornell complies with Iowa's Smoke-free Air Act. Cornell utilizes E-Verify and requires the satisfactory completion of a background check. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws. \nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. About Us You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/COR1036CORN/JobBoard/30d770d7-3983-4bf1-867a-479db251bad8/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=3a095697-d355-4acb-bd78-201aef29e69e": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Math (Part-time)",
      "description": "Lecturer in Math (Part-time) | Career Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Lecturer in Math (Part-time) Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on September 10, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA +0 more locations less locations Faculty Part-Time Requisition #: LECTU001423 Description Cornell College, a private undergraduate liberal arts college in Mount Vernon, Iowa, is seeking a Lecturer in Mathematics for one course.  A Ph.D. in mathematics or a closely related field is preferred; candidates with at least a master’s degree in mathematics or a closely related field will also be considered. Courses and term dates Because Cornell utilizes a block schedule for its courses, you would teach this one course full time during the four-week session. MAT 236 - Differential Equations (Block 6: 2/08/27 - 3/03/27) This course includes mathematical modeling with differential equations, initial value problems and their approximate solutions, systems of differential equations, qualitative solutions, stability analysis and an introduction to chaos, and Laplace transforms. The college encourages interdisciplinary interests among its faculty and the development of teaching strategies that capitalize on our distinctive academic calendar. One Course At A Time allows us the freedom to take students off-campus without impinging on other course commitments. In addition, class size is limited to 24 students, and upper-level courses are often smaller. About Cornell College Cornell College is a national liberal arts college committed to excellence in teaching and the creation of a welcoming community in which all individuals are respected and included. Our innovative curriculum includes a focus on the essential abilities of writing, quantitative reasoning, and intercultural literacy as well as experiential learning. The One Course At A Time approach fosters strong student engagement and close faculty-student relationships while allowing faculty freedom to design and carry out their classes, on campus or off. Founded in 1853, Cornell was the first college west of the Mississippi to graduate both men and women.  Academic immersion, real world experience requirements through Ingenuity in Action, and unparalleled flexibility attract an ambitious student body from around the world.  Seventy percent of our students are from outside Iowa, representing nearly 50 states and 27 foreign countries. Students of color comprise one-fourth of the student body. Cornell’s picturesque hilltop campus is a National Historic District and was the first campus listed in its entirety on the National Register of Historic Places. Mount Vernon is a small, college-centered town in the Cedar Rapids-Iowa City corridor, home to nearly half a million people. It has two additional National Historic Districts and a classic Main Street a short walk from campus. Mount Vernon attractions include boutique shopping; walking paths; a dedicated sledding hill; and 13 annual festivals and events including Chalk the Walk, Chili Cookoff, and Magical Mount Vernon. Interested applicants should submit the following materials through Cornell College’s online application system: A letter of application/cover letter Current Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information for a minimum of two references. Applications will be reviewed as submitted and continue until the position is filled. For more information about the department, please visit the Mathematics and Statistics department website . Any questions can be directed to J. Fabián Candelaria, Co-Chair of Mathematics and Statistics at jcandelaria@cornellcollege.edu. Cornell is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from underrepresented groups. Cornell complies with Iowa's Smoke-free Air Act. Cornell utilizes E-Verify and requires the satisfactory completion of a background check. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws. \nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. About Us You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
    "https://recruiting2.ultipro.com/COR1036CORN/JobBoard/30d770d7-3983-4bf1-867a-479db251bad8/OpportunityDetail?opportunityId=00f20081-af74-4dda-a4aa-4eadfa46d951": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Trainer | Career Opportunities British English CA English Czech Danish Deutsch Dutch Español FR French Français Canadien Hungarian Italian Japanese Korean Polish Português do Brasil Romanian Swedish Thai U.S. English Vietnamese 简体中文 繁體中文 Find Opportunities U.S. English Sign In Assistant Athletic Trainer Share Post on X Apply now Job Details Posting Details Posted on September 3, 2026 Locations Showing 1 location Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA Iowa Cornell Campus 600 1st St SW Mt Vernon, IA 52314, USA +0 more locations less locations Athletics Full-Time Requisition #: ASSIS001420 Description Cornell College invites applications for the position of assistant athletic trainer. The assistant athletic trainer assists the head athletic trainer in all aspects of the athletic training program, including the evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries.  The position also assists with the supervision of the sports medicine assistants and the supervision and operation of the training room.  The position is full-time, 10 months with working dates of August 1 - May 31. Duties & Responsibilities Prevention of athletic injuries/illnesses. Evaluation of athletic injuries/illnesses and medical referral. First aid and emergency care of athletic injuries/illnesses. Rehabilitation and reconditioning of athletic injuries/illnesses. Counseling and guidance of athletes. Educating the sports medicine assistants in areas of athletic training.  Teaching courses in the department of kinesiology, as needed and as assigned by the chair of the kinesiology department and the director of athletics. Coverage of athletic practices and athletic events as assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer. Travel with athletic teams as assigned by Head Athletic Trainer. Coordinates educational sessions for sports medicine assistants. Assist in coordinating proper medical forms and injury reports. Assist with record keeping of all athletic injuries and treatments. Assist in scheduling of doctor’s appointments for injured athletes. Assist with daily inventory of training room supplies. Assist with ordering of training room supplies. Assist in maintaining the departmental emergency plan and equipment. Other duties as assigned. About Cornell College Cornell College is a selective liberal arts college distinguished by our Ingenuity curriculum that builds on the strengths of our One Course At A Time schedule. This combination encourages the qualities of being thoughtful, original, and inventive, using the strengths of a liberal arts education to apply ideas to solve problems and meet challenges through hands-on experience in learning. Academic immersion, Division III NCAA athletic teams, and unparalleled flexibility attract an ambitious student body from across the U.S. and worldwide. We are located in Mount Vernon, Iowa, an urban fringe community located in the heart of the ICR Iowa region. Qualifications and Education Requirements Minimum qualifications include a bachelor's degree and commitment to the values, standards, and expectations of NCAA Division III athletics and a liberal arts college.  National Athletic Trainers’ Association Board of Certification is required.  Must be eligible for a license in the state of Iowa.  Preferred qualifications include CPR and First Aid Instructor Certified, master’s degree and previous experience as a certified athletic trainer. Must have a valid Iowa driver’s license and insurance coverage (if driving own vehicle) or be insurable. Preferred Skills Knowledge and skills in preventing athletic injuries, providing physical examinations, developing training and conditioning programs, selecting protective equipment, creating a safe athletic environment, and evaluating athletic injuries.  Ability to make appropriate medical referrals, providing first aid and emergency care, rehabilitation and reconditioning of athletic injuries, counseling and guidance of athletes, and educating sports medicine assistants. Knowledge of ordering equipment and supplies, record keeping, supervising sports medicine assistants and ability to work collaboratively with student health care providers.  Ability to construct orthotic and protective devices, proficient use of all training room modalities, and to develop and maintain professional medical contacts. Must be self-directed, well organized and capable of assuming varied responsibilities. Administration, management and supervision of employees are key components for the success of this position. Computer knowledge is preferred. Working Conditions Travel is required.  Frequent weekend and evening hours is required.  Working environment includes both indoors and outdoors, exposure to various weather conditions, including temperature extremes. Must have the physical ability to walk, lift up to 50 pounds, run, bend, twist, climb, see, hear, and communicate both verbally and in writing. All requirements are subject to change over time, with possible modifications made to reasonably accommodate individuals with a disability. Cornell College offers a fantastic benefits package that includes health, dental, vision, HSA & FSA accounts, a TIAA 403(b) retirement account, and tuition remission and exchange for employees and dependents. We also offer life insurance, disability insurance, travel insurance, and accident insurance. Application Process To apply, submit a cover letter, resume, and list of at least three professional references through Cornell College's online application system. Cornell is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from underrepresented groups. Cornell complies with Iowa's Smoke-Free Air Act. Cornell utilizes E-Verify and requires satisfactory completion of a background check. Qualifications Skills Behaviors : Motivations : Education Required Bachelors or better in Health and Human Performance. Experience Licenses & Certifications Equal Opportunity Employer This employer is required to notify all applicants of their rights pursuant to federal employment laws. \nFor further information, please review the Know Your Rights notice from the Department of Labor. About Us You are using an unsupported browser. To use this site, please use a supported browser. Download Firefox Download Chrome Download Internet Explorer"
    },
